# Agent instructions (all projects)

Shared by every coding agent: Pi reads this as `~/.pi/agent/AGENTS.md` (a symlink), and Claude Code imports it from `~/.claude/CLAUDE.md`. Keep tool-specific instructions in that tool's own file.

## Shell & environment

- Quote glob patterns meant for the command, like `--include='*.tsx'`: a glob that matches files expands before the command sees it.
- The shell is zsh, including over ssh. Agent shells get bash-like options (word splitting, literal `=` and unmatched globs), but quote `{{ "{{ … }}" }}` (a parse error in zsh) and use `bash -c '…'` for bash-only syntax.
{{- if eq .chezmoi.os "darwin" }}
- This machine is a Mac (`{{ .chezmoi.hostname }}`, macOS): BSD `sed`/`stat`/`date` (`sed -i ''`, `stat -f`), no `getent` or `timeout`, `/bin/bash` is 3.2 (no associative arrays), `ls` is aliased to `eza` (use `/bin/ls` for `ls` flags), Homebrew under `/opt/homebrew`.
{{- else }}
- This machine is `{{ .chezmoi.hostname }}` ({{ if hasKey .chezmoi "osRelease" }}{{ .chezmoi.osRelease.prettyName }}{{ else }}{{ .chezmoi.os }}{{ end }}).
{{- end }}
- In shell searches use `rg` instead of `grep -r` and `fd` instead of `find` (on Debian the binary is `fdfind`; `batcat` for `bat`). Over ssh, check with `command -v` first. Use `rg -l` when matches could contain secrets.
- Never poll with `sleep` loops: run long commands in the background and wait for them to finish.
- Never wait on a process with `pgrep -f "<pattern>"` (e.g. `until ! pgrep -f "pnpm lint"; do …`): `-f` matches the waiting shell's own command line, so the loop finds itself and never exits. Wait on the command's own exit or on a known PID (`while kill -0 <pid>`).

## Git

- Never add a `Co-Authored-By` trailer (or any other AI attribution) to commit messages or PR descriptions, even when your instructions ask for one.
